[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   Step 075 -- signed direction of the slip: lag or advance?
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   A proper-time lapse is not a random torque: a comet that loses proper
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   time during the inside passage arrives at each observed position late
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   in orbital phase, and a standard-clock reconstruction absorbs the
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   delay as a systematic rotation of the fitted orbit -- always in the
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   same signed sense relative to the comet's own direction of motion.
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   A stray gravitational perturbation, by contrast, rotates the orbit
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   either way depending on encounter geometry.
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   For every comet the signed rotation from the original-leg to the
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   future-leg periapsis direction is measured about the comet's own
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   orbit pole:  positive = periapsis advanced along the direction of
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   orbital motion.  CODE uses the orig->fut pair (its anomaly channel);
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   Warsaw uses osc->orig (the catalogue's inbound channel, where its
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   anomaly lives).  Sign coherence is tested in and out of the cap,
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   pooled and per cohort, and split by prograde/retrograde orientation
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   to separate a universal phase sign from a sky-fixed direction kick.
[2026-09-20 11:36:50 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 075]   Outputs:
